Subject: [PATCH] container: avoid constexpr function-address compare in GetPolicyFunctions

Abseil's raw_hash_set::GetPolicyFunctions() initializes a
`static constexpr PolicyFunctions value`. One of its members is
`get_hash_slot_fn<hasher>()`, which compares the address of the function
template `TypeErasedApplyToSlotFn<...>` against nullptr. Some GCC versions
(notably the aarch64-linux-gnu GCC 11 cross toolchain) refuse to treat that
function-address comparison as a core constant expression, so the
`static constexpr` initializer fails to compile:

    hash_policy_traits.h:163:54: error:
      '(... TypeErasedApplyToSlotFn<...> == 0)' is not a constant expression

Making `value` a `static const` instead of `static constexpr` keeps the exact
same semantics (a function-local static initialized once) but no longer forces
constant evaluation of the function-address comparison, so it compiles on the
affected compilers while remaining correct everywhere else.
--- a/absl/container/internal/raw_hash_set.h
+++ b/absl/container/internal/raw_hash_set.h
@@ -4100,5 +4100,5 @@
   static const PolicyFunctions& GetPolicyFunctions() {
-    static constexpr PolicyFunctions value = {
+    static const PolicyFunctions value = {
         sizeof(slot_type),
         // TODO(b/328722020): try to type erase
         // for standard layout and alignof(Hash) <= alignof(CommonFields).
